  <content>
  <section><title>Lesson Narrative</title>
<para>This lesson reinforces the concept of the solution of a system of two linear equations. Students are also asked to write systems of equations from a table of values and connect that to a graph of a system of equations using technology.</para>
<para>Students then write the systems of equations from a graph and solve the system using the graph. In the cool down, students will explore how a system of equations represents a real world problem.</para>
<para>Making internet-enabled devices available gives students an opportunity to choose appropriate tools strategically.</para>
<title>Learning Goals (Teacher Facing)</title>
<para>Students will be able to: </para>
<list>
  <item> Write a system of equations from a table of values, a graph, and a verbal description. </item>
  <item> Graph systems of equations by hand and determine solutions. </item>
  <item> Estimate solutions to real-world problems by graphing systems of equations. </item>
</list>
<title>Learning Targets (Student Facing)</title>
<list>
  <item> Write a system of equations. </item>
  <item> Graph systems of equations by hand. </item>
  <item> Estimate real-world solutions by graphing systems of equations. </item>
</list>
